<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ua Fáeláin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ó Faoláin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ua Fáeláin were the ruling family of the Déisi of Munster, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-waterford">County Waterford</a> and south Tipperary, in the 11th and 12th centuries. They took their name from an ancestor called Fáelán. Their kingdom was overrun when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Normans</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a> in 1170, and their name survives in the modern surnames Phelan and Whelan.</p></div>
